cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below. If you use
  the archived research evidence under research/, also cite the exact release and
  the third-party sources your analysis relies on.
title: "ComputerUseAgent: browser and X11 interaction trace recorder and human-vs-agent evaluation toolkit"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yan
    given-names: Weiping
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/appleweiping/ComputerUseAgent"
url: "https://github.com/appleweiping/ComputerUseAgent"
abstract: >-
  ComputerUseAgent is a consent-first toolkit for recording and analysing
  computer-use interaction traces. It contains a Chrome Manifest V3 extension
  that stores privacy-reduced browser interaction traces locally, an X11 capture
  path, JSON Schemas for the trace and dataset formats, a standard-library
  Python package that extracts 23 behavioral features and runs a deterministic,
  leakage-aware human-vs-agent evaluation pipeline, and a loopback-only trace
  viewer. No validated human-vs-agent detector is claimed; the archived research
  evidence documents what was and was not measured.
keywords:
  - computer-use agents
  - interaction traces
  - human-vs-agent detection
  - browser extension
  - behavior measurement
  - reproducibility
